    <skos:altLabel>Chain-growth polymerization</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A chain-growth polymerization is a type of polymerization where monomers are added to an active center one by one to form an oligomer or polymer. I.e. the polymer grows one monomer at a time</skos:definition>
