    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000908"/>
    <skos:altLabel> </skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Flame dry is a process where a piece of vessel is dried (remove residual moisture or solvent) using a flame. This is commonly done in reactions where presence of moisture in the vessel during the reaction will negatively impact the outcome (i.e. lower yield, degradation of reagents, etc.).</skos:definition>
