    <skos:altLabel> </skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A reaction time is a temporal interval of a chemical reaction process that is a one-dimensional temporal region that is continuous, thus without gaps or breaks. The period of time that elapses between the start of the reaction and the attainment of a given extent of a reaction. [IUPAC]</skos:definition>
    <mds:hasStudyStage>Synthesis</mds:hasStudyStage>
