    <skos:altLabel>VoltageOpenCircuit</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>voc</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>A characterization method for solar cells that measures the open-circuit voltage (Voc) as a function of incident light intensity, expressed in suns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition>The open circuit voltage measured by a current voltage process.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition>Voltage potential across the postive and negative terminal under irradiation when zero current flows in or out of the terminals.</skos:definition>
    <mds:hasStudyStage>Characterization</mds:hasStudyStage>
    <mds:hasStudyStage>Result</mds:hasStudyStage>
    <mds:hasStudyStage>Sample</mds:hasStudyStage>
