    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000908"/>
    <skos:altLabel> </skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In a chemical reaction context, compound preparation is an act of artifact processing during which a compound (i.e. a component of a reaction) is prepared (e.g. dried, repurified) for a reaction. This step is frequently necessary as many compounds from suppliers are not in desired conditions for a reaction.</skos:definition>
